[Chapter "Slow Slav (4.e3)"]
[Line "Nh4 grabs the bishop"]
[Opening "Slav Defense: Quiet Variation, Schallopp Defense"]

{White plays a calm e3 and then hunts the f5 bishop with the knight.} 1. d4 d5 {Claim the centre.} 2. c4 {The Queen's Gambit: White attacks d5.} 2... c6 {The Slav: support d5 with a pawn and keep the c8 bishop's diagonal open, unlike ...e6.} 3. Nf3 Nf6 {Develop and guard d5 again.} 4. e3 {The quiet approach: support d4 and c4.} 4... Bf5 {Bishop out before ...e6, as always in the Slav.} 5. Nc3 e6 {Now close the pawn chain behind the bishop.} 6. Nh4 {White goes after the bishop to win the bishop pair.} 6... Bg6 {Keep the bishop on its good diagonal for now.} 7. Nxg6 hxg6 {Recapture with the h-pawn: Black's rook gets the half-open h-file, and the doubled pawns are hard to attack.} *
